          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em Walker-Wang model
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+%28in+theoretical+physics%29"} model (in theoretical physics)
            which is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/4d+TQFT"} 4d TQFT
            analog of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Levin-Wen+model"} Levin-Wen model
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3d+TQFT"} 3d TQFT
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian"} Hamiltonian
            formulation of the TQFT whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+function"} partition function
            formulation is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Crane-Yetter+model"} Crane-Yetter model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+insulators"} topological insulators
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/solid+state+physics"} solid state physics
